# Shared build-cache location for this box. Copy to cache.env (git-ignored):
#
#   cp cache.env.example cache.env    # then edit BS_CACHE_DIR below
#
# The Makefile loads cache.env via `-include` (so this is Makefile syntax, not
# shell). Set an ABSOLUTE path; a relative value resolves against the repo root.
#
# If BS_CACHE_DIR is left unset here: the Makefile auto-discovers the sibling
# ../argus-all/argus-build-cache when it holds a built SDK, else cache.sh falls
# back to ../argus-build-cache.
#
# The cache is built once per box by the brightsign-sdk-builder repo and reused
# across our NPU extensions -- see docs/PRE-REQS.md.
#
# Example (reuse the shared argus build cache):
# BS_CACHE_DIR := /home/you/src/brightsign-playground/argus-all/argus-build-cache
#
# --- Auto-build the SDK when the cache is empty (optional) ---
# If the configured cache has no SDK, `make build`/`make fetch-sdk` build it via
# brightsign-sdk-builder automatically (needs Docker + network + ~25GB; hours).
#   BS_SDK_AUTOBUILD := 0        # disable auto-build; print manual instructions
#   SDK_BUILDER_DIR  := /abs/path/to/brightsign-sdk-builder   # skip auto-discovery/clone
